{
 "thread": "IOAUfKEOR_I",
 "subject": "cfa output in lavaan not showing all the items for modification indices",
 "messages_listed": 7,
 "last_activity": "2019-05-16T20:07:42Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "YT2FiXWKAwAJ",
   "from": "Seun Kolade",
   "author": "8f4d54d40a591ec9",
   "date": "2019-05-14T07:48:35Z",
   "subject": "cfa output in lavaan not showing all the items for modification indices",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello everyone,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m currently running a cfa model on lavaan. The modification indices items are not all showing. Lavaan says 183 rows are missing, I suppose due to the limit on the number of items that can be displayed. Is there a way I can see these remaining items? I think they may give me the information I need to covary the relevant indicator error terms.</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks,</div><div>Seun</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "-uDzxJqLAwAJ",
   "from": "Seun Kolade",
   "author": "8f4d54d40a591ec9",
   "date": "2019-05-14T08:09:35Z",
   "subject": "cfa output in lavaan not showing all the items for modification indices",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Just a quick update. I’ve now figures out how to do this by using the SORT argument and setting to minimum of 15- to take out the smaller values."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "F_4v4OoTAgAJ",
   "from": "car...@web.de",
   "author": "5abdb409f213d464",
   "date": "2019-05-14T08:15:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: cfa output in lavaan not showing all the items for modification indices",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>From my point of view, this has nothing to do with lavaan. With options you can influence the output behavior of R.  Regardless, I don&#39;t think you really need all modification indices results. Probably it&#39;s enough to look at the really relevant results like this:<br>\r\nmi &lt;- modindices(fit) <br>\r\nmi[mi$mi &gt; 10,]<br>\r\n10 is arbitrary, of course.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "WZn7UbB7BAAJ",
   "from": "Christopher David Desjardins",
   "author": "189d19347ab44a74",
   "date": "2019-05-16T19:40:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: cfa output in lavaan not showing all the items for modification indices",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Tue, May 14, 2019 at 3:15 AM <a href=\"http://mailto:car...@web.de\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:car...@web.de&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423755533000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nvHesvOqJ0t8a8QyBKwLS\">car...@web.de</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>From my point of view, this has nothing to do with lavaan. </div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This is correct. It’s an option in R, max.print.  </p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(lavaan)\r\nmodel &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&#39; \r\n  # latent variable definitions\r\n     ind60 =~ x1 + x2 + x3\r\n     dem60 =~ y1 + a*y2 + b*y3 + c*y4\r\n     dem65 =~ y5 + a*y6 + b*y7 + c*y8\r\n\r\n  # regressions\r\n  QA.GMF =~ ind60:dem60\r\n    dem65 ~ QA.GMF\r\n&#39;</span>\r\n\r\nfit &lt;- sem(model, data=PoliticalDemocracy)\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># play around with printing settings, note this doesn&#39;t</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\"># have to do with lavaan</span>\r\noptions()$max.print\r\noptions(max.print = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">100</span>)\r\nmodindices(fit)\r\noptions(max.print = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">500</span>)\r\nmodindices(fit)\r\noptions(max.print = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1000</span>)\r\nmodindices(fit)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>With options you can influence the output behavior of R.  Regardless, I don&#39;t think you really need all modification indices results. Probably it&#39;s enough to look at the really relevant results like this:<br>\r\nmi &lt;- modindices(fit) <br>\r\nmi[mi$mi &gt; 10,]<br>\r\n10 is arbitrary, of course.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
